message:
Looks like I broke the responsive theme somehow.  

Not sure WTF I did. response.css has a bug....

We should look like this:

[img]https://i.imgur.com/N12y7Cg.png[/img]

Instead we look like this:

[img]https://i.imgur.com/H1sP4EX.png[/img]


The forums are pushed down.  Inline-block screwed up.

What did I change. There was a typo in the css as td-foat-right, changed it to td-float-right. I attempted top undo the changes. No good.

Frustrating.  It still seems fine on the old BLUE MOBALE theme for some reason but we've done many edits.

One difference from an issue in convo is this css:

In blue it's: 
.mobile-link-truncate {
	display: table-cell;
	overflow: hidden;
	text-overflow: ellipsis;
}

That was changed because of convo fix....

It's now....

.mobile-link-truncate {
	text-overflow: ellipsis;
        word-break: break-word;
        overflow-wrap: anywhere;
}

I just added a definition to response.css and changed the name of the css in the template, didn't seem to work. 

.mobile-link-truncate-forum {
	display: table-cell;
	overflow: hidden;
	text-overflow: ellipsis;
}

10k bytes to anyone who can fix the theme css without breaking some other element.


HELP! Any CSS pro who can figure this out asap?  Will also grant an award too.
